<[Doug] D.PHILIPS2> Not in 'C', but I think I have pseudo-code for DO ... LOOP.
<[Doug] D.PHILIPS2> #define sign(x)  ((x) < 0 ? (-1) : 1)
<[Doug] D.PHILIPS2> int s = sign( index - limit );
<[Doug] D.PHILIPS2> for( ; s == sign( index - limit ); index += loop_incr) body;
<[Wil] W.BADEN1> I dont think so.
<[Wil] W.BADEN1> In fact I dont think it can be done with C's "for".
<[Doug] D.PHILIPS2> C's for is just a while loop!
<[Wil] W.BADEN1> DO...LOOP is a "do ... while (cond);" loop.
<[Doug] D.PHILIPS2> Because of at least once execution semantics.
<[Wil] W.BADEN1> Yes.
<[Wil] W.BADEN1> But even F83 ?DO...LOOP cannot be done as "for(...)"
